WEBVTT

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:17.990
The sea at twilight.

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:19.410
The calls of the gulls.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.120
Just a little tinted pale.

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.920
Never let me see you again!

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.720
Marie, don't be so cold!

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.580
Cold or warm isn't the problem!

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:38.760
Then what is?

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:41.520
I don't have any money left to lend you.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.020
Enough already.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.490
Jeez, what a loser.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.250
Aww, don't be like that.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:47.490
My bank account is empty!

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.510
But if you sold the shop...

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.990
That wasn't a smart thing to say.

00:00:55.570 --> 00:00:59.280
Shut up! This shop's the 
only thing I have left!

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.080
And besides... whose fault 
do you think that is?

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:44.690
Are you all right?

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.650
I'm sorry, my mom's terribly violent...

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:51.270
I'm totally fine.

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.930
Not even a little hurt.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:54.340
Not even a scratch.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:00.330
I think you might actually be hurt!

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.430
Hey, Mom,

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:16.050
she's hungry! Make her something!

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.250
Mom!

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:18.920
Here.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:23.650
I shall accept, thanks. 
I am very grateful, yes.

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:24.930
Thanks for your kindness.

00:03:26.060 --> 00:03:27.230
It says there's pasta.

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:29.310
What kinds of pasta, 
do you sell at this cafe?

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:33.540
We've got carbonara,
carbonara and carbonara.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:37.570
From the sound of it, 
all you have is carbonara.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:40.440
I have no choice, then.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:41.650
I will partake of a meal

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:42.450
of carbonara.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.080
Oh my shooting stars.

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:54.880
This establishment here is

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:56.330
really disgusting.

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:15.900
Hey, hey.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.980
What's your name?

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:19.780
I'm Ai.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:20.980
You would know my name?

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:22.430
It is Matsuo Basho.

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:23.440
That's what they call me.

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:24.310
Basho?

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:25.570
That's a strange name.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:28.150
Hey, hey, Basho-chan.

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:29.620
Do you have a place to stay tonight?

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:32.910
We've got a motel next door.

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:34.370
Why not stay there?

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.230
A motel you say.

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:37.450
I've a very bad feeling

00:04:37.450 --> 00:04:38.750
about your motel...

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:41.670
Hey, it's okay if she stays, isn't it, Mom?

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:47.160
If you didn't say no, 
that means yes, right?

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:48.180
Okay, it's decided, then.

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:50.960
That's surprising.

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:54.500
But I bet she leaves tomorrow.

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:55.770
Oh, fine.

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.330
I bet she never leaves.

00:04:57.820 --> 00:05:00.190
I'm probably gonna lose.

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:03.280
Basho-chan, this is 
the key to your room.

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:05.370
Room 202.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:18.310
Would you look at that?

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:19.610
I knew this was coming, but...

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:20.710
this is terrible.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:39.660
The moon shines down on

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:41.140
this miserable hovel.

00:05:41.140 --> 00:05:42.150
It never changes.

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:48.920
Why?

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:50.920
Why did this have to happen?

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:53.780
I've said this time and time again.

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:55.950
You need to be more forward-thinking.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:57.780
Forward-thinking?!

00:05:57.780 --> 00:06:00.040
Which way is forward for me?

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:01.720
Which way, I wonder.

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:03.900
Anyway, he's a loser.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:05.920
He'd be a terrible dad for Ai-chan.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.420
I think it's for the best.

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:08.620
I dunno.

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:09.620
You think?

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:12.370
So this is a new beginning for me?

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:14.890
That's right! That's right!

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:16.870
Then let's have a toast!

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:18.510
You've drunk enough already.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:19.960
That's enough for today.

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:21.680
I've got a part-time job tomorrow.

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.410
You're so cold.

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:26.520
You can stay here a bit longer.

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:30.000
Oops, I left the bathwater on.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.370
I've gotta get back.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:32.410
You're lying!

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:33.610
You're running away!

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:34.830
I'm not lying!

00:06:40.510 --> 00:06:42.080
Suddenly water

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:43.440
falls upon my sleeping face

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:44.780
from heaven above?

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.970
The water's overflowing!

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.090
I'm soaked!

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:51.590
What do I do? What do I do?

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:11.240
The sad creaking of

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:12.710
the settling timber makes me

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:14.250
sorrow just like it.

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.040
Results Report

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:22.040
<b>DID NOT PASS</b>

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:23.850
The singing voice brings

00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:25.330
with it much melancholy

00:07:25.330 --> 00:07:27.150
I feel so lonely.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:36.420
The run-down motel,

00:07:36.420 --> 00:07:37.570
stains on the ceiling

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:38.810
from the bathroom above me.

00:07:40.470 --> 00:07:44.210
<i>In a way, this place interests me.</i>

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:50.570
What is this?!

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:54.280
The moon hangs in the sky.

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:55.500
It makes a funny sight.

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:03.010
What are you doing?!

00:08:03.010 --> 00:08:04.230
That is my face not a sheet

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:05.210
of writing paper!

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:06.380
What am I doing?

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:07.950
That's my line.

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:09.340
What is all this?

00:08:18.560 --> 00:08:19.650
I cleaned the room.

00:08:19.650 --> 00:08:20.710
That is all that I did.

00:08:20.710 --> 00:08:21.910
Not a thing more.

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:25.960
Take out all the trash,

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:27.230
clean the counters wash the floors,

00:08:27.230 --> 00:08:28.360
you feel much better.

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:30.400
Why are you correcting yourself?

00:08:30.400 --> 00:08:32.370
God, you're annoying.

00:08:32.370 --> 00:08:33.570
Five-seven-five is

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:34.750
what it has to be or I

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:36.170
just do not feel right.

00:08:36.170 --> 00:08:37.910
What the heck?

00:08:39.480 --> 00:08:41.920
Is this really the Far End Cafe?

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:43.380
It's pretty!

00:08:43.380 --> 00:08:45.420
Anyway, change it back now.

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:48.600
I liked it that way!

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:50.920
I can't work like this.

00:08:50.920 --> 00:08:52.530
You've gotta be kidding me.

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:53.910
She's just being stubborn.

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:55.010
Oh, Mom...

00:08:55.330 --> 00:08:57.230
Change it back now.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:08:59.260
A beautiful and

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:00.630
polished workplace makes the heart

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:01.770
feel much more at ease.

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:08.980
Don't touch that!

00:09:10.980 --> 00:09:12.100
Ouch! Ouch! Oww! Oww!

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:13.150
Let me go! Let me go!

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:14.620
Let me go right this instant!

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:15.750
Get out!

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:20.800
She got thrown out. 
Didn't see that coming.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:23.140
Does that mean I win?

00:09:23.140 --> 00:09:24.460
Wait, Mom!

00:09:24.460 --> 00:09:26.730
Don't kick Basho-chan out!

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:31.050
No. She's a guest and 
she messed with my shop.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:32.240
That's not true!

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:36.140
Isn't it nice to have 
the store all clean?

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:37.890
You guys think so too, right?

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:42.990
Well, clean is better than dirty.

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:43.890
Yeah.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:48.280
I want her to clean up 
the motel rooms, too.

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:49.320
Ai...

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:50.700
The girl is quite right.

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:51.880
Listen to your daughter and

00:09:51.880 --> 00:09:52.820
what she has to say.

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:56.740
That haiku crap is pissing me off.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.140
I cannot help it.

00:09:58.140 --> 00:09:59.400
I am a poet and this

00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:00.450
is how I must talk.

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:02.150
A poet?

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:04.220
Like limericks and stuff?

00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:07.460
No, a real poet who writes haikus.

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:09.230
Come on, Mom!

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:11.630
Let her clean the motel rooms!

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:15.380
If you're not okay with that, 
then at least let her clean my room...

00:10:17.060 --> 00:10:18.480
Whatever.

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:20.010
Thank you, Mom!

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:21.970
Basho-chan, will you do it?

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:23.450
Leave it to me.

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:24.560
I know a lot when it

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:26.920
comes to cleaning.

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:30.990
That wasn't five-seven-five at all.

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:32.150
Think too much about

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:33.570
the little things and luck will

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:35.110
fly away from you.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:36.210
Shut up!

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:37.150
However!

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:39.910
Do not touch that piano.

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:09.270
FAR END CAFE

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:11.560
FAR END CAFE

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:17.010
It's like a new building.

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:20.290
The Far End Cafe is reborn.

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:21.500
From now on there will

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:22.760
be customers beating down

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:24.070
a path to your door.

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:26.620
I wonder if we'll get lots of guests.

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:28.520
I know we will!

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:34.800
A little flower.

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:36.170
The water brings with it a

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:37.320
new season of growth.

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:54.440
Oh jeez, so busy! So busy!

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:56.070
Here you are.

00:11:56.870 --> 00:11:59.900
Haiku have their rules. Rules you must 
always follow. You must remember.

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:02.770
Let's begin with this:

00:12:02.770 --> 00:12:04.010
I'll now recite a haiku.

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:05.150
It's five-seven-five.

00:12:06.220 --> 00:12:09.020
Use seasonal words. 
Feel the seasons in your poem.

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:09.870
Don't forget this part.

00:12:11.090 --> 00:12:12.400
A haiku without

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:13.810
seasonal words is known as

00:12:13.810 --> 00:12:15.290
what we call senryu.

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:20.960
Interested in haiku?

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:22.930
Of course not.

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:25.000
You should come out and admit it.

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:29.920
Anyway, this is totally 
a haiku cafe now.

00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:33.980
Yeah. But people love it, 
so it's for the better, right?

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:38.940
And besides, I've begun taking 
an interest in haiku, too.

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:41.190
You too, Kyo-chan?

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:44.320
I always thought of 
them as more musty...

00:12:44.870 --> 00:12:48.550
But trying to follow the rules while you

00:12:48.550 --> 00:12:52.890
express how you feel is a lot of fun.

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:53.830
Yeah.

00:12:54.780 --> 00:12:56.710
Hey, you two.

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:58.960
Stop slacking and get back to work.

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:03.400
She's the one who needs 
haiku more than anybody.

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:04.650
Seriously.

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:06.970
She's stubborn and obstinate.

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:11.970
Oh, yeah.

00:13:11.970 --> 00:13:14.260
Sorry to do this when we're busy,

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:16.410
but can I have tomorrow off?

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:18.350
Got an audition?

00:13:18.350 --> 00:13:22.580
Yup. I don't know what 
I owe the good luck to,

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:24.810
but I made it past the first round!

00:13:24.810 --> 00:13:26.240
That's amazing!

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:30.490
I see. So you're trying to be a dancer.

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:32.700
You thought I was

00:13:32.700 --> 00:13:37.430
just a maid and a dance 
teacher for old ladies.

00:13:37.430 --> 00:13:38.780
That's not true at all...

00:13:40.820 --> 00:13:43.590
You can't think of the 
next line, can you?

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:49.820
Lately, those haiku...

00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:52.190
Well, I guess mine are senryu...

00:13:52.190 --> 00:13:54.060
They've given me an outlet for all

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:57.500
the things I had been building 
up at the bottom of my heart.

00:13:57.500 --> 00:13:59.710
I feel a lot better.

00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:02.320
I'm glad to hear that.

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:03.670
It makes me happy to hear

00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:04.990
you tell me those words.

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:11.010
I think it's the same with Kyo-chan.

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:14.040
When I'd first met him, 
he'd put down his brush.

00:14:14.780 --> 00:14:17.790
But lately, he's started painting again.

00:14:20.950 --> 00:14:24.560
I was just running from everything,

00:14:24.560 --> 00:14:27.720
but now I think it's time to 
start facing into the wind.

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:29.600
Face into the wind.

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:31.180
The wind blows your hair aside

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:32.300
showing your forehead.

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:33.680
Splendid.

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:35.080
Thanks.

00:14:35.800 --> 00:14:39.270
I wish Marie would give the haiku thing a go.

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:42.690
Kyo-chan's got his painting.

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:43.940
I've got my dancing.

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:47.550
But Marie ran away from 
playing the piano.

00:14:48.030 --> 00:14:49.200
Without interest

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:51.110
it is impossible to

00:14:51.110 --> 00:14:52.560
make a real haiku.

00:14:58.720 --> 00:15:00.150
Hello?

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:02.040
Yes.

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:04.560
Just a second.

00:15:04.560 --> 00:15:06.910
Mom, it's somebody from the TV station!

00:15:09.230 --> 00:15:11.370
Hey, I heard!

00:15:11.370 --> 00:15:13.100
Somebody's coming for a TV interview?

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:15.350
The whole town's abuzz!

00:15:15.350 --> 00:15:18.260
More importantly, Satocchan, 
what about your audition?

00:15:18.260 --> 00:15:19.850
Oh, yeah...

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:22.000
<i>If you didn't get</i>

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:23.340
<i>the part, how do we make you...</i>

00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:24.960
<i>...not feel so awful?</i>

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:28.440
I got the part!

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:30.860
That's great!

00:15:30.860 --> 00:15:31.990
You did it!

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:33.280
<i>We didn't believe...</i>

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:34.510
<i>...you would pass the audition.</i>

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:35.700
<i>I'm totally stunned!</i>

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:39.550
Forget that. This TV thing is huge!

00:15:39.550 --> 00:15:42.960
Haiku are amazing, aren't they, Mom?!

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:53.040
Drink up the water.

00:15:53.040 --> 00:15:54.330
Grow up big and grow up tall.

00:15:54.330 --> 00:15:55.220
Happy and cheerful.

00:16:04.460 --> 00:16:05.930
I'd love to hear it.

00:16:05.930 --> 00:16:07.660
The sound of the piano,

00:16:07.660 --> 00:16:08.930
that you used to play.

00:16:08.930 --> 00:16:11.050
Nobody asked you!

00:16:11.050 --> 00:16:14.480
I'm never... never playing 
the piano again.

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:19.870
Mom! The TV people are here!

00:16:24.690 --> 00:16:26.150
Oh what have I done...

00:16:26.150 --> 00:16:27.390
I shouldn't have said a word.

00:16:27.390 --> 00:16:28.380
That would have been best.

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:32.800
FAR END CAFE

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:32.800
Special

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:32.800
<b>An experience you can only get here.

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:33.380
<i>Today, we're here at the Far End Cafe,</i>

00:16:33.380 --> 00:16:36.400
<i>which has been popular 
lately as a haiku cafe.</i>

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:38.720
<i>So you're the owner, right?</i>

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:40.310
<i>H-Hello there!</i>

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:43.070
It's Mom! Mom's on TV!

00:16:43.070 --> 00:16:44.080
She is so nervous

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:45.600
that her voice is quivering,

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:46.680
our Marie-san.

00:16:46.680 --> 00:16:47.880
Shaddup.

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:50.280
How many times are you gonna 
watch that recording?

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:51.580
I want to watch it over and over.

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:54.010
<i>Basho-chan taught us haiku.</i>

00:16:54.010 --> 00:16:55.930
<i>Everyone's enjoying it.</i>

00:16:54.010 --> 00:16:57.740
Oh no, it's true! 
You look fatter on TV!

00:16:57.740 --> 00:17:00.840
And the shadow on my cheeks 
isn't working at all!

00:17:00.840 --> 00:17:03.830
Really? You don't look 
any different to me.

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:06.150
What's that supposed to mean?!

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:08.860
Is that a compliment or an insult?

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:10.370
Welcome!

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:11.490
One customer...

00:17:15.690 --> 00:17:16.740
Satoshi...

00:17:17.920 --> 00:17:19.100
Mom.

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:24.470
Satoshi... I finally found you.

00:17:28.450 --> 00:17:29.750
Face into the wind

00:17:29.750 --> 00:17:31.210
The wind blows your hair aside

00:17:31.210 --> 00:17:32.650
Showing your forehead.

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:36.870
Satoshi...

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:42.820
Mom...

00:17:42.820 --> 00:17:44.440
Satoshi...

00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:47.360
Mother and child unite.

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:48.810
The gulls dancing in the sky

00:17:48.810 --> 00:17:50.060
They are happy, too.

00:17:51.480 --> 00:17:53.320
All thanks to the power of television.

00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:56.410
I guess the haiku cafe isn't...

00:17:56.410 --> 00:17:58.030
The haiku cafe, isn't what?

00:17:58.030 --> 00:17:59.440
Never mind.

00:17:59.440 --> 00:18:02.100
Isn't so bad, is that what 
you were going to say?

00:18:03.730 --> 00:18:05.800
I said never mind!

00:18:05.800 --> 00:18:07.600
Now get to work!

00:18:08.120 --> 00:18:10.540
She's really so stubborn.

00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:37.490
So she wants to hear me 
play the piano, huh?

00:18:53.210 --> 00:18:54.900
The Far End Cafe:

00:18:54.900 --> 00:18:56.610
Such a fun place to live at.

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:57.950
I bid thee farewell.

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:04.370
I guess you're enjoying 
your life here, Basho.

00:19:04.810 --> 00:19:06.120
Nobunaga!

00:19:06.550 --> 00:19:08.060
I have to talk to you.

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:09.990
I wouldn't want us to be interrupted,

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:12.380
so I'd like to talk alone.

00:19:12.380 --> 00:19:13.710
Can you leave now?

00:19:18.560 --> 00:19:21.700
I guess the haiku cafe isn't...

00:19:21.700 --> 00:19:23.460
The haiku cafe, isn't what?

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:24.690
Never mind.

00:19:24.690 --> 00:19:26.990
"Isn't so bad."

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:29.990
Why couldn't I say it?

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:43.370
Basho?

00:19:50.010 --> 00:19:51.270
Bats are out at night.

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:52.680
They, too, are birds, and their cries

00:19:52.680 --> 00:19:54.040
adorn the night sky.

00:19:55.790 --> 00:19:57.860
Basho!

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:02.140
Wait!

00:20:02.140 --> 00:20:03.380
Basho!

00:20:03.380 --> 00:20:04.680
Where are you going?

00:20:04.960 --> 00:20:06.470
Huh? What? Marie?

00:20:06.470 --> 00:20:08.030
Why is it that you try and

00:20:08.030 --> 00:20:09.340
stop me here, right now?

00:20:09.340 --> 00:20:12.100
Your haiku buddy?

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:13.640
I dunno.

00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:16.550
Could she be my haiku buddy?

00:20:21.220 --> 00:20:22.240
What?

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:25.400
Are you gonna just do 
all that and then leave?

00:20:25.400 --> 00:20:26.980
Wait!

00:20:26.980 --> 00:20:28.740
You still have stuff to do!

00:20:29.300 --> 00:20:33.410
Teach me... Teach me haiku, too!

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:35.250
It's my cafe!

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:37.220
It doesn't make sense that

00:20:37.220 --> 00:20:40.020
I'm the only one who doesn't 
know how to write haiku!

00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:43.070
I...

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:47.810
I want you to be here!

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:55.030
Jeez... if you were going to leave... 
if you were going to leave...

00:20:56.350 --> 00:20:58.510
You never should've come.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:10.170
"The Far End Cafe:

00:21:10.170 --> 00:21:12.010
Such a fun place to live at.

00:21:12.010 --> 00:21:14.080
I bid thee farewell."

00:21:17.520 --> 00:21:20.600
That's even sadder.

00:21:35.190 --> 00:21:38.760
Um... what kinds of pasta can you make?

00:21:38.760 --> 00:21:42.150
Peperoncino, vongole bianco, and rosso.

00:21:42.470 --> 00:21:45.400
And genovese and arrabiata.

00:21:45.820 --> 00:21:48.470
Anything you want, really.

00:21:48.470 --> 00:21:49.870
Carbonara.

00:21:56.400 --> 00:21:57.760
The carbonara

00:21:57.760 --> 00:21:59.050
is the best in all the world

00:21:59.050 --> 00:22:00.320
I love it so much!

00:22:06.240 --> 00:22:07.990
The Far End Cafe:

00:22:07.990 --> 00:22:11.440
It's the place where I belong.

00:22:12.360 --> 00:22:13.510
Wrong number of syllables!

00:23:45.820 --> 00:23:47.180
The next episode

00:23:47.180 --> 00:23:50.180
features the regent girl, 
Toyotomi Hideyoshi.

00:23:50.180 --> 00:23:51.570
Way too many syllables.

00:23:52.240 --> 00:23:55.700
Next time on Sengoku 
Collection: "Regent Girl."

00:23:55.700 --> 00:23:56.850
Saying all my lines

00:23:56.850 --> 00:23:58.440
in five-seven-five is hard.

00:23:58.440 --> 00:23:59.880
I am exhausted.
